$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Cross-coupling reaction: Inside the glovebox S5a (77.0 mg, 200 μmol) and
Ni(dppe)Cl2 (3.2 mg, 6 μmol, 3%) were weight into a reaction tube, 1 mL
THF was added, followed by addition of a solution of o-anisy
ZnBr·LiBr·2.5 THF (311 mg, 600 μmol) in 9 mL of THF. The reaction tube
was equipped with a stirring rod, sealed and stirred at ambient
temperature until the catalyst had completely dissolved (ca. 5 minutes).
The reaction mixture was then stirred at 50 °C for 1 h and heated briefly
to reflux (10 min). The reaction was then quenched by addition of 1 mL of
methanol, the solvent was removed and the residue was extracted with
dichloromethane. The concentrated extract was directly subjected to
column chromatography (SiO2, hexanes/ethyl acetate, 10:1, v/v). The
product obtained as that crystallized upon standing.
2,5-bis(o-anisyl)-4-(triisopropylsilyloxymethyl)thiazol, pale colorless
oil, yield 26.5 mg, 54.4 μmol, 27 %.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube used, glovebox used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Soluble Head-to-Tail Regioregular Polythiazoles: Preparation, Properties,
and Evidence for Chain-Growth Behavior in the Synthesis via
Kumada-Coupling Polycondensation
