$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for Iron-catalyzed coupling
reactions (Table 1). 3-bromo-2-pyrone 3 or 3-triflyl-2-pyrone 7 (0.123
mmol) and Fe(acac)3 (5 mol%) were dissolved in a mixture of THF/NMP
(0.62:0.11 mL) and the mixture was cooled to 0 °C. The Grignard reagent
(0.221 mmol, 1.8 equiv.) was added dropwise, and the reaction was stirred
at 0 °C for 5 minutes, after which it was quenched with saturated NH 4 Cl
solution (2 mL). The aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O (2 × 5 mL),
EtOAc (5 mL), and the combined organic layers were washed with saturated
NaHCO3 solution (5 mL) and water (5 mL), dried (MgSO4) and the solvent
was removed under reduced pressure. Purification was achieved by flash
chromatography on a silica gel column with pentane/ethyl acetate or ether
as eluant. Entry 3, compound 4c. Yield = 33%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM 33% conversion, Grignard reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Concise Access to 3-Substituted 2-Pyrones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
