$DATUM Kumada coupling of 3,6-dibromothieno[3,2-b]thiophene. Reaction protocol:
3,6-dibromothieno[3,2-b]thiophene (0.220 mmol; 66.2 mg) and Ni(dppp)Cl2
(2 mol%; 2.39 mg) were combined in a flask, brought under argon
atmosphere and dissolved in dry Et2O (2.00 mL). To this mixture,
n-butylmagnesiumchloride (0.22 mL; 2.00 M in THF) was added dropwise.
After a reaction time of 2 hours, an aliquot of the reaction was washed
with water to remove the salts and the organic layer was analyzed with
GC-MS. Compound: 3,6-dibromothieno[3,2-b]thiophene.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Kumada coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Evidence for Catalyst Association in the Catalyst Transfer Polymerization
of Thieno[3,2-b]thiophene
